From 606a765523bcba66fbb1e1c060bfb15bee685fe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:46:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: decode all-gathers by multirank RoCE writes
 (TF_GLM_ROCE_MESH)

At three ranks or more a decode window's layer exchanges went through
NCCL's ring (W - 1 hops). With TF_GLM_ROCE_MESH=1 they go through
fabric/tp's multirank gather: each rank's shard written once to every
peer, flags polled by the copy-out kernel. On six GB10s over one 200G
switch (tf-tp-test suite, world 6) 16 / 32 / 64 KiB a rank take
23 / 28 / 36 us against NCCL's 52 / 80 / 86.

cuda_mesh.zig brings it up after the group: fabric/tp's bootstrap and
HCA pick (TF_TP_MASTER, TF_TP_PORT, TF_TP_ROCE_HCA), the mailbox fatbin
from TF_TP_KERNEL_IMAGE, then a patterned probe gather checked on every
rank; any rank's failure leaves every rank on NCCL. Prompt chunks and
gathers past the slot stay on NCCL. glm_cuda imports tp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
